            <ArticleTitle>Small bowel intussusception with pelvic plastron secondary to acute appendicitis in child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E5-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpedsurg.2009.12.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report an unusual case of a 3-year-old child with appendicitis complicated by ileoileal intussusception. Although acute complicated appendicitis and concurrent ileoileal intussusception represent a possible cause of an acute abdomen, very few cases have been reported in the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
